### Justification
The claim that Paul Pogba quit the French national team over Emmanuel Macron’s remarks on Islam is refuted. No official announcement was made by Pogba or the French Football Federation, and Pogba himself publicly dismissed the report as "fake news" ([Hindustan Times](https://www.hindustantimes.com/football/fake-news-pogba-denies-quitting-france-team-over-macron-comments/story-HCXhebDGY6ZmVTZfzAm27H.html)). He continued to play for France in October 2020, after Macron’s October 2 statement ([Goal](https://www.goal.com/en/news/pogba-brands-reports-of-imminent-retirement-from-international-football-fake-news/tj0phkyxy1vl1ntvurrj36um2)). Major outlets did not corroborate the claim, and no evidence of a mass protest or boycott among other players was found ([Zeebiz](https://www.zeebiz.com/world/news-paul-pogba-reportedly-quits-playing-for-france-after-president-emmanuel-macrons-islam-mention-138073)).